> Time: 1423492646 / Mon, 09 Feb 2015 14:37:26 +0000
> URL: /index.php?/REST/Forums/topic/getPosts?topicId=78412&start=10&SessionId=bcb3fc5a5bb5832db4628a145aed1177
> User headstand (276487)
Request Time: 0 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"174.119.162.30","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78412,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"bd9535665a0cbad59db60dbef9e0b322","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Ours came out to about $1680 from Toronto for 1 week at Beach Palace in Cancun, airport transfers and direct flight with Air Canada.&amp;nbsp; Our week is right before Christmas so rates weren&#039;t crazy high season prices yet, but they weren&#039;t low either.&amp;nbsp; Unfortunately I couldn&#039;t really be flexible about the dates because I&#039;m in school again this year and I had to arrange it for a week I have off, or wait until I&#039;m done in May (which I wasn&#039;t willing to wait for before haha.&amp;nbsp; Now I&#039;m like oh shoot, it all came so fast ahhh!)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We also had some complaints about it being so close to Christmas and some people complained about the price, but as all of the ladies said above, the people that are going to come regardless will come through for you! We may have had a few more people had we waited until May or if we had chosen a cheaper resort, but ultimately we had to put our desires first because it is our wedding!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I&#039;m not too familiar with Cuba but I think it&#039;d be a bit cheaper than Mexico.&amp;nbsp; Good luck w\/ your planning! Definitely find a good TA&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1879032,"PostDate":1416778991,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Ours came out to about $1680 from Toronto for 1 week at Beach Palace in Cancun, airport transfers and direct flight with Air Canada.\u00a0 Our week is right before Christmas so rates weren't crazy high season prices yet, but they weren't low either.\u00a0 Unfortunately I couldn't really be flexible about the dates because I'm in school again this year and I had to arrange it for a week I have off, or wait until I'm done in May (which I wasn't willing to wait for before haha.\u00a0 Now I'm like oh shoot, it all came so fast ahhh!)<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We also had some complaints about it being so close to Christmas and some people complained about the price, but as all of the ladies said above, the people that are going to come regardless will come through for you! We may have had a few more people had we waited until May or if we had chosen a cheaper resort, but ultimately we had to put our desires first because it is our wedding!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm not too familiar with Cuba but I think it'd be a bit cheaper than Mexico.\u00a0 Good luck w\/ your planning! Definitely find a good TA<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>45 guests + bride & groom <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My Planning Thread - <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77763-tygrrlilys-planning-thread-beach-palace-resort-121914\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77763-tygrrlilys-planning-thread-beach-palace-resort-121914\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My Wedding Review<\/p>\n<p>Part 1 - <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77763-tygrrlilys-planning-thread-beach-palace-resort-121914\/?p=1881197'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77763-tygrrlilys-planning-thread-beach-palace-resort-121914\/?p=1881197<\/a><\/p>\n<p>Part 2 - <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77763-tygrrlilys-planning-thread-beach-palace-resort-121914\/?p=1881590'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77763-tygrrlilys-planning-thread-beach-palace-resort-121914\/?p=1881590<\/a><\/p>\n<p>Part 3 - <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77763-tygrrlilys-planning-thread-beach-palace-resort-121914\/?p=1881861'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77763-tygrrlilys-planning-thread-beach-palace-resort-121914\/?p=1881861<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Post Wedding Sale - <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78637-post-wedding-sale-gold-pinks-coral-ivory-black-and-white-stripe\/#entry1883373'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78637-post-wedding-sale-gold-pinks-coral-ivory-black-and-white-stripe\/#entry1883373<\/a>","Email":"lilyluu83@gmail.com","IpAddress":"174.119.162.30","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1395580548,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277296.jpg?_r=1421643766","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"tygrrlily","Id":277296,"Name":"tygrrlily","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78412,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":4,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"dc761c1fad8972fcae78b09d50c7ae8a","RawContent":"[quote name=\"tygrrlily\" post=\"1879032\" timestamp=\"1416807791\"]\nOurs came out to about $1680 from Toronto for 1 week at Beach Palace in Cancun, airport transfers and direct flight with Air Canada.  Our week is right before Christmas so rates weren&#039;t crazy high season prices yet, but they weren&#039;t low either.  Unfortunately I couldn&#039;t really be flexible about the dates because I&#039;m in school again this year and I had to arrange it for a week I have off, or wait until I&#039;m done in May (which I wasn&#039;t willing to wait for before haha.  Now I&#039;m like oh shoot, it all came so fast ahhh!)\n\nWe also had some complaints about it being so close to Christmas and some people complained about the price, but as all of the ladies said above, the people that are going to come regardless will come through for you! We may have had a few more people had we waited until May or if we had chosen a cheaper resort, but ultimately we had to put our desires first because it is our wedding!\n\nI&#039;m not too familiar with Cuba but I think it&#039;d be a bit cheaper than Mexico.  Good luck w\/ your planning! Definitely find a good TA[\/quote]\nI don&#039;t think you can win no matter what you do -- it&#039;s too close to Christmas, it&#039;s too soon after Christmas, it&#039;s too close to Easter, it&#039;s too close to my great grandma&#039;s sister&#039;s brother&#039;s cousin&#039;s communion hahahah!!    You can only do the best you can do!","Attachments":[],"Id":1879039,"PostDate":1416809566,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>tygrrlily, on 23 November 2014 - 09:43 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>Ours came out to about $1680 from Toronto for 1 week at Beach Palace in Cancun, airport transfers and direct flight with Air Canada.\u00a0 Our week is right before Christmas so rates weren't crazy high season prices yet, but they weren't low either.\u00a0 Unfortunately I couldn't really be flexible about the dates because I'm in school again this year and I had to arrange it for a week I have off, or wait until I'm done in May (which I wasn't willing to wait for before haha.\u00a0 Now I'm like oh shoot, it all came so fast ahhh!)<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We also had some complaints about it being so close to Christmas and some people complained about the price, but as all of the ladies said above, the people that are going to come regardless will come through for you! We may have had a few more people had we waited until May or if we had chosen a cheaper resort, but ultimately we had to put our desires first because it is our wedding!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm not too familiar with Cuba but I think it'd be a bit cheaper than Mexico.\u00a0 Good luck w\/ your planning! Definitely find a good TA<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I don't think you can win no matter what you do -- it's too close to Christmas, it's too soon after Christmas, it's too close to Easter, it's too close to my great grandma's sister's brother's cousin's communion hahahah!! \u00a0 \u00a0You can only do the best you can do!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399399802,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"65.95.204.5","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78412,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":3,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"572c2352c041a95840696f6d5a9d9d93","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;We searched for a good few months and I drove myself crazy trying to figure out pricing and best resorts. I spoke to a couple TA&#039;s before finding a good one that my fiance and I vibed well with.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Our main priorities were budget friendly, decent\/or free basic wedding packages, and a place where we could get legally married without doing blood tests or anything too nuts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We started looking early and were SUPER flexible with months\/dates. We were originally thinking Nov 2014 but we creeped closer to that date and found that prices in Jan\/Feb and May were comparable for the resorts we looked at.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Our TA let us know that Mexico and Cuba are the most cost effective generally from Toronto. There&#039;s always exceptions to this rule of course. We ended up with a 4.5* in Cuba for $973 double and $1133 single taxes in.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1879155,"PostDate":1416922335,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>We searched for a good few months and I drove myself crazy trying to figure out pricing and best resorts. I spoke to a couple TA's before finding a good one that my fiance and I vibed well with.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Our main priorities were budget friendly, decent\/or free basic wedding packages, and a place where we could get legally married without doing blood tests or anything too nuts.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We started looking early and were SUPER flexible with months\/dates. We were originally thinking Nov 2014 but we creeped closer to that date and found that prices in Jan\/Feb and May were comparable for the resorts we looked at.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Our TA let us know that Mexico and Cuba are the most cost effective generally from Toronto. There's always exceptions to this rule of course. We ended up with a 4.5* in Cuba for $973 double and $1133 single taxes in.\u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"jannahurren@gmail.com","IpAddress":"50.101.125.237","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1396266542,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277424.jpg?_r=1401464547","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":113,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"jlc3","Id":277424,"Name":"jlc3","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"184.69.200.21","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78412,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"3a5406e5c0bfddc277a533100eb5cb10","RawContent":"[quote name=\"jlc3\" post=\"1879155\" timestamp=\"1416951135\"]\nWe searched for a good few months and I drove myself crazy trying to figure out pricing and best resorts. I spoke to a couple TA&#039;s before finding a good one that my fiance and I vibed well with.\n\nOur main priorities were budget friendly, decent\/or free basic wedding packages, and a place where we could get legally married without doing blood tests or anything too nuts. \n\nWe started looking early and were SUPER flexible with months\/dates. We were originally thinking Nov 2014 but we creeped closer to that date and found that prices in Jan\/Feb and May were comparable for the resorts we looked at. \n\nOur TA let us know that Mexico and Cuba are the most cost effective generally from Toronto. There&#039;s always exceptions to this rule of course. We ended up with a 4.5* in Cuba for $973 double and $1133 single taxes in.[\/quote]I LOVED Cuba, have you been before?","Attachments":[],"Id":1879156,"PostDate":1416922693,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>jlc3, on 25 November 2014 - 01:32 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>We searched for a good few months and I drove myself crazy trying to figure out pricing and best resorts. I spoke to a couple TA's before finding a good one that my fiance and I vibed well with.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Our main priorities were budget friendly, decent\/or free basic wedding packages, and a place where we could get legally married without doing blood tests or anything too nuts.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We started looking early and were SUPER flexible with months\/dates. We were originally thinking Nov 2014 but we creeped closer to that date and found that prices in Jan\/Feb and May were comparable for the resorts we looked at.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Our TA let us know that Mexico and Cuba are the most cost effective generally from Toronto. There's always exceptions to this rule of course. We ended up with a 4.5* in Cuba for $973 double and $1133 single taxes in.\u00a0<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>I LOVED Cuba, have you been before?<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399399802,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"99.244.52.21","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78412,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"b7517e94b014301a875148315032773c","RawContent":"That&#039;s what I&#039;m talking about! Lol. Which resort did you pick?","Attachments":[],"Id":1879177,"PostDate":1416944338,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                That's what I'm talking about! Lol. Which resort did you pick?\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"empty_xo@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"99.244.52.21","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1416668737,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Brandii","Id":281229,"Name":"Brandii","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"71.7.173.185","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78412,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"3762040e09b0660d5670af52aac292c8","RawContent":"[quote name=\"jlc3\" post=\"1879155\" timestamp=\"1416951135\"]\nWe searched for a good few months and I drove myself crazy trying to figure out pricing and best resorts. I spoke to a couple TA&#039;s before finding a good one that my fiance and I vibed well with.\n\nOur main priorities were budget friendly, decent\/or free basic wedding packages, and a place where we could get legally married without doing blood tests or anything too nuts. \n\nWe started looking early and were SUPER flexible with months\/dates. We were originally thinking Nov 2014 but we creeped closer to that date and found that prices in Jan\/Feb and May were comparable for the resorts we looked at. \n\nOur TA let us know that Mexico and Cuba are the most cost effective generally from Toronto. There&#039;s always exceptions to this rule of course. We ended up with a 4.5* in Cuba for $973 double and $1133 single taxes in. \n\nYES, I&#039;d love to know where your resort is too :)[\/quote]","Attachments":[],"Id":1879208,"PostDate":1417020322,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>jlc3, on 25 November 2014 - 01:32 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>We searched for a good few months and I drove myself crazy trying to figure out pricing and best resorts. I spoke to a couple TA's before finding a good one that my fiance and I vibed well with.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Our main priorities were budget friendly, decent\/or free basic wedding packages, and a place where we could get legally married without doing blood tests or anything too nuts.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We started looking early and were SUPER flexible with months\/dates. We were originally thinking Nov 2014 but we creeped closer to that date and found that prices in Jan\/Feb and May were comparable for the resorts we looked at.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Our TA let us know that Mexico and Cuba are the most cost effective generally from Toronto. There's always exceptions to this rule of course. We ended up with a 4.5* in Cuba for $973 double and $1133 single taxes in.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>YES, I'd love to know where your resort is too <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"njwood000@gmail.com","IpAddress":"71.7.173.185","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1405795991,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"Msmimi","Id":279087,"Name":"Msmimi","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"71.202.225.11","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78412,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"8b47743e58ef58c804443221398c7fa9","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;pricing is really going to depend on a few factors:&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;1. there is a big price difference between high and low seasons&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;2. how many nights? &amp;nbsp;This is going to factor in because if some people are quoting 3 nights vs. 7 nights, obviously that is going to make a difference.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;3. are there any charter flights out of your area?&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;4. the quality of resort. &amp;nbsp;A 4 star will be much higher than a 2 star&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;5. All-inclusive vs. non-AI. &amp;nbsp;Upfront the cost may be lower for a non-AI but once you factor in food and drinks, AI are usually a better route.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;6. Location: usually cabo and riviera maya are more expensive than PV but once you factor in air it changes which is more expensive. &amp;nbsp;Dominican republic is a good option as well if you have good, direct air.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;There is a reason why Riviera Maya\/Cancun is one of the most popular dw spots. You get great bang for your buck.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1879239,"PostDate":1417084265,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>pricing is really going to depend on a few factors:<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>1. there is a big price difference between high and low seasons<\/p>\n<p>2. how many nights? \u00a0This is going to factor in because if some people are quoting 3 nights vs. 7 nights, obviously that is going to make a difference.<\/p>\n<p>3. are there any charter flights out of your area?<\/p>\n<p>4. the quality of resort. \u00a0A 4 star will be much higher than a 2 star<\/p>\n<p>5. All-inclusive vs. non-AI. \u00a0Upfront the cost may be lower for a non-AI but once you factor in food and drinks, AI are usually a better route.<\/p>\n<p>6. Location: usually cabo and riviera maya are more expensive than PV but once you factor in air it changes which is more expensive. \u00a0Dominican republic is a good option as well if you have good, direct air.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>There is a reason why Riviera Maya\/Cancun is one of the most popular dw spots. You get great bang for your buck.<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Founder and Owner of BestDestinationWedding.com<\/span><br>\u00a0<br><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/wrighttravelagency.com\/inquiry\/'><span style=\"color:#008080;\">Looking for a travel agency that specializes in Destination Weddings<\/span><\/a><\/strong><span style=\"color:#008080;\"><strong>?<\/strong> \u00a0We are an award winning travel agency and you can <\/span><strong><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/reviews\/p\/21494-wright-travel-agency-destination-wedding-and-honeymoon-specialists\/'><span style=\"color:#008080;\">read our reviews\u00a0here.<\/span><\/a><\/strong><\/span><br>\u00a0<br><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"color:#008080;\"><strong>Awards and recognition:\u00a0<\/strong><\/span><\/span><br><span style=\"color:#008080;\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Palace Resorts PRO Platinum Agency (Top Award) \u00a0 \u00a0 | \u00a0 \u00a0<\/span><\/span><span style=\"color:#008080;\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">AMResorts Master Agent & Top Agency \u00a0<\/span><\/span><br><span style=\"color:#008080;\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Karisma Hotels Diamond Level 5 (highest production), Top 10 Azul Weddings, Top Wedding Coordinator | <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/68050-karisma-hotels-givc-and-gi-wedding-consultants-wright-travel-agency\/'><strong>Wright Travel & Karisma GIVC Benefits<\/strong><\/a><\/span><\/span><br><span style=\"color:#008080;\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Travel Impressions Best of the Best Globe Winner \u00a0 \u00a0| \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0<\/span><\/span><span style=\"color:#008080;\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Apple Vacations Golden Apple Winner \u00a0<\/span><\/span><br><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.phpgallery\/image\/75243-karisma-diamond-level-5\/\" title=\"Karisma Diamond Level 5\"><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_8442\/sml_gallery_206696_8442_4984.png' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='Karisma Diamond Level 5'  width='200' height='200'  alt='Karisma Diamond Level 5' id='sml_image_view_75243' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><span style=\"font-size:14px;\"><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.phpgallery\/image\/77453-pro-palace-specialist-agent-platinum-sm\/\" title=\"PRO PALACE SPECIALIST AGENT PLATINUM Sm\"><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17572\/sml_gallery_206696_17572_2474.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='PRO PALACE SPECIALIST AGENT PLATINUM Sm'  width='200' height='118'  alt='PRO PALACE SPECIALIST AGENT PLATINUM Sm' id='sml_image_view_77453' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/span><br><span style=\"color:#008080;\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\"><strong><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/921\/vendor-business-membership-fees-rules-updated-6-18-2010'>Vendor rules are HERE! Please read!<\/a>\u00a0\u00a0<\/strong><\/span><\/span><\/span><strong><span style=\"color:#b22222;\">If you are a vendor and looking to advertise your business,<\/span>\u00a0please email\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='mailto:ads@bestdestinationwedding.com?subject=Advertising%20on%20BestDestinationWedding.com'>ads@bestdestinationwedding.com<\/a>.<\/strong>","Email":"admin@bestdestinationwedding.com","IpAddress":"71.202.225.11","GroupId":4,"GroupName":"Administrators","JoinDate":1137195420,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-206696.jpg?_r=1386394555","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":135,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"TammyWright","Id":206696,"Name":"TammyWright","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.57.1","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78412,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"b60f9d4f9045f33deab536fc4d261370","RawContent":"I&#039;m going to throw this out there - you will end up disappointed with pricing of you compare group rates to last minute rates. That was super hard for me to wrap my head around, but once I got past that, I was able to commit! From calgary we paid $1700 all in for a week at the now Amber in puerto Vallarta  in November. I got rates from a few agents, and a few suppliers and made sure I got the best rate I could find - I didn&#039;t have much flexibility with dates. Puerto Vallarta is getting more expensive.\n\n\nSomething else to consider (which a good Tavel agent will help you with) is the incentives from the different suppliers. Since you have 15ppl you may not qualify for huge incentive, but may get a room of two free.\n\nYou could always apply that incentive over everyone&#039;s package to make prices cheaper for your guests. Also pay very close attention to the wedding packages at each resort. Some offer way better packages than other and you don&#039;t want to screw yourself by choosing a cheaper package for your guests.\n\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1879502,"PostDate":1417529677,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                I'm going to throw this out there - you will end up disappointed with pricing of you compare group rates to last minute rates. That was super hard for me to wrap my head around, but once I got past that, I was able to commit! From calgary we paid $1700 all in for a week at the now Amber in puerto Vallarta  in November. I got rates from a few agents, and a few suppliers and made sure I got the best rate I could find - I didn't have much flexibility with dates. Puerto Vallarta is getting more expensive.<br><br>\nSomething else to consider (which a good Tavel agent will help you with) is the incentives from the different suppliers. Since you have 15ppl you may not qualify for huge incentive, but may get a room of two free.<br>\nYou could always apply that incentive over everyone's package to make prices cheaper for your guests. Also pay very close attention to the wedding packages at each resort. Some offer way better packages than other and you don't want to screw yourself by choosing a cheaper package for your guests.<br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"chelseapjohnson@yahoo.ca","IpAddress":"70.72.57.238","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1361465668,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-266402.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":150,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"chelseapaige37","Id":266402,"Name":"chelseapaige37","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"71.17.38.13","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78412,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"cf357633f6be13f929d148b95010ee49","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"chelseapaige37\"] What airline did you use? Is that price with taxes included? That sounds like a good price! I&#039;m in the process of getting Now Amber\/Secrets Vallarta quoted for the week. What did you think of the beach area at Now Amber by the way? Thanks!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1879587,"PostDate":1417619344,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"266402\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/266402-chelseapaige37\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">chelseapaige37<\/span><\/a> What airline did you use? Is that price with taxes included? That sounds like a good price! I'm in the process of getting Now Amber\/Secrets Vallarta quoted for the week. What did you think of the beach area at Now Amber by the way? Thanks!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"penjani@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"71.17.38.13","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1393146302,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"peachykeen159","Id":276833,"Name":"peachykeen159","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.57.1","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78412,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1417622348,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"29b106f604d23835a7caddae18a999da","RawContent":"[quote name=\"peachykeen159\" post=\"1879587\" timestamp=\"1417648144\"]\n@[member=\"chelseapaige37\"] What airline did you use? Is that price with taxes included? That sounds like a good price! I&#039;m in the process of getting Now Amber\/Secrets Vallarta quoted for the week. What did you think of the beach area at Now Amber by the way? Thanks![\/quote]\nYes that included taxes! We made sure everyone booked to get the early booking bonuses which helped. We went with Air Canada Vacations - you can always email their groups department - our agent has quoted us like $500 more for the same package. That may be sneaky of me but o didn&#039;t understand why it was so high. Your agent will have to price match it. We ended up getting $2750 back from the am resorts room comps.  \n\nThe beach area isn&#039;t great but it didn&#039;t bother me. We actually stayed for 2 weeks and I didn&#039;t go into the ocean until the last day - it was beautiful! Wish k has spent more time in it. It was red flagged the entire two weeks but ppl swam almost every day. I personally didn&#039;t find the undertow that bad. There are vendors who will try to sell you goods and drugs - but they leave you alone if you say no. We are pool ppl so spent most of our time there - our friends are beach ppl and said it was fine. I absolutely LOVED the now amber. I think we will return for our anniversary next year! \n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1879593,"PostDate":1417622277,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>peachykeen159, on 03 December 2014 - 03:09 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'><p>\n@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"266402\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/266402-chelseapaige37\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">chelseapaige37<\/span><\/a> What airline did you use? Is that price with taxes included? That sounds like a good price! I'm in the process of getting Now Amber\/Secrets Vallarta quoted for the week. What did you think of the beach area at Now Amber by the way? Thanks!<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n<br><br>\nYes that included taxes! We made sure everyone booked to get the early booking bonuses which helped. We went with Air Canada Vacations - you can always email their groups department - our agent has quoted us like $500 more for the same package. That may be sneaky of me but o didn't understand why it was so high. Your agent will have to price match it. We ended up getting $2750 back from the am resorts room comps.  <br><br>\nThe beach area isn't great but it didn't bother me. We actually stayed for 2 weeks and I didn't go into the ocean until the last day - it was beautiful! Wish k has spent more time in it. It was red flagged the entire two weeks but ppl swam almost every day. I personally didn't find the undertow that bad. There are vendors who will try to sell you goods and drugs - but they leave you alone if you say no. We are pool ppl so spent most of our time there - our friends are beach ppl and said it was fine. I absolutely LOVED the now amber. I think we will return for our anniversary next year! <br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"chelseapjohnson@yahoo.ca","IpAddress":"70.72.57.238","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1361465668,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-266402.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":150,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"chelseapaige37","Id":266402,"Name":"chelseapaige37","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":59,"TotalPages":6,"CurrentPage":10,"NextPage":20,"PreviousPage":0,"LastPage":50},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
