{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":true,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":63282,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1387282757,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"b197079d6281c5ad31cfec9d11edd19a","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;This is the new OFFICIAL Gran Bahia Principe Riviera Maya Thread!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Here you will find the answer to almost all of your questions!&amp;nbsp; If you don&#039;t see the answer, feel free to ask, but please look through the information first. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663888&#039;&gt;Post #2&lt;\/a&gt; - Basic Information (Resort Info, Contact Info, Legal Requirements)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663889&#039;&gt;Post #3&lt;\/a&gt; - Wedding Packages&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663891&#039;&gt;Post #4&lt;\/a&gt; - Wedding Locations&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663892&#039;&gt;Post #5&lt;\/a&gt; - Dinner Locations, Options &amp;amp; Cost&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663893&#039;&gt;Post #6&lt;\/a&gt; - DJ Options and Costs&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663894&#039;&gt;Post #7&lt;\/a&gt; - Cake&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663895&#039;&gt;Post #8&lt;\/a&gt; - Details (ceremony details, hacienda stuff, random questions and answers)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663896&#039;&gt;Post #9&lt;\/a&gt; - Flowers&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663897&#039;&gt;Post #10&lt;\/a&gt; - Spa&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread\/10#post_1663898&#039;&gt;Post #11&lt;\/a&gt; - Arrecife Studio (the onsite photographers)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread\/10#post_1663899&#039;&gt;Post #12&lt;\/a&gt; - Wedding Reviews&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread\/10#post_1663900&#039;&gt;Post #13&lt;\/a&gt; - Wedding Photos &amp;amp; Video Links&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread\/10#post_1663901&#039;&gt;Post #14&lt;\/a&gt; - Resort Reviews&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread\/10#post_1663902&#039;&gt;Post #15&lt;\/a&gt; - Bride Roll Call!&amp;nbsp; Shoot me a PM with your user name, wedding date, and dates you&#039;ll be at the resort (ie: tlseege, 4\/11\/2008, 4\/7-4\/14) and I&#039;ll add you to the list&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread\/10#post_1663903&#039;&gt;Post #16&lt;\/a&gt; - Faber Photography&#039;s Photo Tours&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread\/10#post_1663904&#039;&gt;Post #17&lt;\/a&gt; - Reserved for future use &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Again, if you have anything to add to this, please feel free to send me a PM or shoot me an email and I will gladly update the thread.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; The old &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/786\/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here&#039;&gt;Gran Bahia Thread&lt;\/a&gt; is still alive and active, but hopefully that thread will be more for brides to discuss their weddings and form a sense of community. &amp;nbsp; Thanks!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1514319,"PostDate":1314944056,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>This is the new OFFICIAL Gran Bahia Principe Riviera Maya Thread!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Here you will find the answer to almost all of your questions!\u00a0 If you don't see the answer, feel free to ask, but please look through the information first. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663888' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #2<\/a> - Basic Information (Resort Info, Contact Info, Legal Requirements)<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663889' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #3<\/a> - Wedding Packages<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663891' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #4<\/a> - Wedding Locations<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663892' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #5<\/a> - Dinner Locations, Options & Cost<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663893' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #6<\/a> - DJ Options and Costs<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663894' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #7<\/a> - Cake<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663895' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #8<\/a> - Details (ceremony details, hacienda stuff, random questions and answers)<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663896' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #9<\/a> - Flowers<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread#post_1663897' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #10<\/a> - Spa<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread\/10#post_1663898' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #11<\/a> - Arrecife Studio (the onsite photographers)<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread\/10#post_1663899' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #12<\/a> - Wedding Reviews<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread\/10#post_1663900' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #13<\/a> - Wedding Photos & Video Links<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread\/10#post_1663901' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #14<\/a> - Resort Reviews<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread\/10#post_1663902' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #15<\/a> - Bride Roll Call!\u00a0 Shoot me a PM with your user name, wedding date, and dates you'll be at the resort (ie: tlseege, 4\/11\/2008, 4\/7-4\/14) and I'll add you to the list<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread\/10#post_1663903' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #16<\/a> - Faber Photography's Photo Tours<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/75549\/official-gran-bahia-principe-riviera-maya-thread\/10#post_1663904' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #17<\/a> - Reserved for future use \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Again, if you have anything to add to this, please feel free to send me a PM or shoot me an email and I will gladly update the thread.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0 The old <a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/786\/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here' class='bbc_url' title=''>Gran Bahia Thread<\/a> is still alive and active, but hopefully that thread will be more for brides to discuss their weddings and form a sense of community. \u00a0 Thanks!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"~Trisha~<br \/>\n<a class='bbc_url' href='http:\/\/www.faberphotography.com'>www.faberphotography.com<\/a><br \/>\n<br \/>\nMy latest destination wedding photos can be found <a class='bbc_url' href='http:\/\/faberphotography.com\/destination-wedding\/'>HERE<\/a>","Email":"tfaber@wbmi.com","IpAddress":"12.24.226.126","GroupId":46,"GroupName":"VIP Member","JoinDate":1171980900,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-207201.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Tlseege","Id":207201,"Name":"Tlseege","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":63282,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"5d3bde3d1ed275572f55f9ae412ebb4b","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\"Gran Bahia Riviera Maya Map\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/532516\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Here is a new 2011 map of the resort, including the golf facility across the road.&amp;nbsp; To view it zoomed, go &lt;img alt=\"Gran Bahia 2011 Resort Map\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/589575\/width\/600\/height\/450\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"http:\/\/www.locogringo.com\/maps\/tour\/bahia-p-t.html\"&gt;http:\/\/www.locogringo.com\/maps\/tour\/bahia-p-t.html&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/786\/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here\/1890#post_1001258\"&gt;Post # 1897&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Tulum&lt;\/u&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Tulum was the first hotel of the complex with 858 rooms, only 84 junior suites and the rest of them standard rooms&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Wedding Coordinator is Jazmin - &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"mailto:grupostulum@tulum.bahia-principe.com\"&gt;grupostulum@tulum.bahia-principe.com&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Wedding Sites: Beach, Gazebo&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Wedding Dinner Choices: Tequila or Gran Tortuga&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Akumal&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/u&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Akumal was the second in built with 630 rooms, 72 standard and 558 junior suites&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Wedding sites:&amp;nbsp; Hammocks, Garden&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Rain location:&amp;nbsp; Akumal Lobby Bar, Club Coba (deceiving name, as it\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s actually in the basement of the Akumal Lobby)&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Wedding Dinner choices: Dolce Vita (Italian) and Frutos Del Mar (Fish)&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Coba&lt;\/u&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Coba the last one built with 1080 rooms all junior suites&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Wedding sites: Choice between Akumal and Tulum locations&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Wedding Coordinator - Karla &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"mailto:groupmx3@bahia-principe.com\"&gt;groupmx3@bahia-principe.com&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/786\/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here\/2230#post_1092530\"&gt;Post #2238 - Distance to beach\/Akumal area\/etc&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; \n &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/786\/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here\/70#post_166597\"&gt;Wedding Applications you&#039;ll be asked to fill out.&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/786\/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here\/150#post_240868\"&gt;Welcome Packet from a previous bride&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Day Passes are $90 USD for guests who aren&#039;t staying at the hotel or vendors such as hair and makeup.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Local outside photographers are NOT allowed, however you can fly in your photographer and have them stay at the resort as a guest.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Legal Requirements for those not previously married:&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Passport, tourist card, blood tests &amp;amp; four witnesses (and their passports &amp;amp; tourist cards)&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Valid passports. In case the bride&#039;s name is not the same in her passport than in her birth certificate and she wants to get married with the same name of her birth certificate she should bring her birth certificate (original) apostilled by the government of her country and translated into Spanish by a Mexican official translator (stamped). Driver license will not be accepted by the official.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; If the bride is widowed or divorced is necessary to bring her birth certificate (original) apostilled by the government of her country and translated into Spanish by a Mexican official translator (stamped), according to Mexican Law the bride must be 12 months divorced before remarrying.&lt;span style=\"font-size: 12px\"&gt; &lt;span style=\"color: #333333\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: tahoma\"&gt;In case the bride\u00b4s name is the same as her maiden name in the passport \u00e2\u20ac\u201c she can use the passport as official ID and will marry as single ( In Mexico after being divorce the marital status is single) \u00e2\u20ac\u201c no translations of birth certificate are required.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12px\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"color: #333333\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: tahoma\"&gt;If the groom is widowed or divorced, no additional documents are required (as his name did not change)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Tourist Card. Travelers get this card upon arrival at the airport in Mexico.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Medical Documentation: Blood tests (Sexually Transmitted diseases - VDRL, HIV, Blood Type) and medical certification stating that all results were negative and patient is physically in good health. Blood tests have to be done here in Mexico, we have a clinic at the Resort - (approximate cost: 90.00 USD per person paid IN CASH).&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Four witnesses: two for the bride and two for the groom with valid passport. The witnesses have to be older than 18 years. All witnesses must come in person to the appointment with the wedding coordinator with their valid passport and tourist card at least 4 labor days prior to the wedding date.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/786\/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here\/1940#post_1007105\"&gt;Post #1945 - It&#039;s really THAT easy!&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;strong&gt;UK Legal Requirements (updated 8\/17\/2012):&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p id=\"yui_3_4_1_1_1345220679318_446\"&gt; Deed Poll (if you have changed your name)&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p id=\"yui_3_4_1_1_1345220679318_445\"&gt; Adoption Certificate (even if only adopted by step father\/mother)&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p id=\"yui_3_4_1_1_1345220679318_440\"&gt; Birth Certificates (even from the person who has an adoption certificate).&amp;nbsp;In the UK (not sure about other countries) the adoption certificate super seeds the birth certificate... this means that the birth certificate can not be used for any legal &amp;nbsp;purpose.. But the Mexican authorities require it... the general registry office in London is very reluctant to produce on of these, but will in the end.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Ala Carte Information:&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; If guests stays for 4 or 7 nights how many nights can they eat at the a la cart restaurant?&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; 3 or 4 nights 1 dinner&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; 5 or 6 nights 2 dinners&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; 7 or 9 nights 3 dinners&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; If you take the dinner included in the wedding package, that counts as one of your guests ala carte meals.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Random Information:&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; The bars located by the pool and beach area close at 5:00 pm , bars located in the lobby from 10 am till 11:00 pm Music Bar from 6:30 pm till 10:30 pm , Bars located at Hacienda Do\u00b1a Isabel from 7:00 pm till midnight and Disco from midnight till 2:00 am&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Everything is paid for at the end of your stay, and they do accept credit cards. (Except the blood work, that is in cash at the time of your appointment)&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; The internet access is at the Hacienda so you have to pay in cash (it can&#039;t be charged to the room - I don&#039;t think). I used it once for under 10 minutes and I think it was close to $7-8 (so about $1\/min). I don&#039;t remember exactly though. I paid in USD but they take pesos too.&amp;nbsp; Diamond club members get free internet access in the lobby.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Brides and Grooms are given Gold bracelets, my family all were \"Gold class\" but got yellow bracelets. As it was explained to us, actual gold bracelets are VIP. They do not keep track of your a la cartes.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Rehearsals aren\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t done at this resort.&amp;nbsp; But the coordinators will not let you screw up.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Legal ceremonies cannot be altered and must be read in Spanish and translated to English.&amp;nbsp; You can add readings or sand ceremony type items after the legal portion has been completed.&amp;nbsp; This can either be read by the translator or a guest.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/786\/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here\/1360#post_743274\"&gt;Here is a post where some additional random questions are answered&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/786\/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here\/1360#post_743274\"&gt;Here too.&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Hotel safe = $6 extra a day.&amp;nbsp; Some people have gotten this as a perk, some people haven&#039;t.&amp;nbsp; Just be prepared to pay it and be pleasantly surprised if you don&#039;t have to.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Mosquitoes in October\/November&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; All three resorts now use key cards instead of traditional keys.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Hurricane Information:&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; In 2011 Tropical Storm Rina hit the Gran Bahia.&amp;nbsp; In the days leading up to landfall it was a Hurricane 2 and then a 1.&amp;nbsp; One of our brides was visiting the resort at this time has reported back:&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; \"I have never been exposed to really bad weather there and have to say the Bahia kept us well informed about the path of the storm and how that would affect the hotel and guests. They prepared for the worst but it ended up being not too bad. They pulled the hurricane shutters, evacuated Building 66 at Akumal (right on the beach), removed all lounge chairs from the beach and pool areas, removed signage\/garbage cans etc that could be blown around or damaged.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; They removed strips of thatching from the Grand Tortuga roof to allow the wind to blow through...and then repaired it when the storm passed.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p id=\"yui_3_4_1_3_1321279261041_21\"&gt; They did the same thing with the Premier Lobby bordering Coba and Akumal. It was good to experience how they handle such weather\/storms...I always felt safe and well informed.\"&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1514320,"PostDate":1314944067,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"Gran Bahia Riviera Maya Map\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/532516\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> Here is a new 2011 map of the resort, including the golf facility across the road.\u00a0 To view it zoomed, go <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"Gran Bahia 2011 Resort Map\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/589575\/width\/600\/height\/450\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> <a href='http:\/\/www.locogringo.com\/maps\/tour\/bahia-p-t.html' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/www.locogring...\/bahia-p-t.html<\/a><\/p> <p> <a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/786\/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here\/1890#post_1001258' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post # 1897<\/a><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <strong><u>Tulum<\/u><\/strong><\/p> <p> Tulum was the first hotel of the complex with 858 rooms, only 84 junior suites and the rest of them standard rooms<\/p> <p> Wedding Coordinator is Jazmin - <a href='mailto:grupostulum@tulum.bahia-principe.com' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>grupostulum@tulum.bahia-principe.com<\/a><\/p> <p> Wedding Sites: Beach, Gazebo<\/p> <p> Wedding Dinner Choices: Tequila or Gran Tortuga<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <u><strong>Akumal<\/strong><\/u><\/p> <p> Akumal was the second in built with 630 rooms, 72 standard and 558 junior suites<\/p> <p> Wedding sites:\u00a0 Hammocks, Garden<\/p> <p> Rain location:\u00a0 Akumal Lobby Bar, Club Coba (deceiving name, as it\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s actually in the basement of the Akumal Lobby)<\/p> <p> Wedding Dinner choices: Dolce Vita (Italian) and Frutos Del Mar (Fish)<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <strong><u>Coba<\/u><\/strong><\/p> <p> Coba the last one built with 1080 rooms all junior suites<\/p> <p> Wedding sites: Choice between Akumal and Tulum locations<\/p> <p> Wedding Coordinator - Karla <a href='mailto:groupmx3@bahia-principe.com' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>groupmx3@bahia-principe.com<\/a><\/p> <p> <a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/786\/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here\/2230#post_1092530' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #2238 - Distance to beach\/Akumal area\/etc<\/a><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <br \/> <a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/786\/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here\/70#post_166597' class='bbc_url' title=''>Wedding Applications you'll be asked to fill out.<\/a><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/786\/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here\/150#post_240868' class='bbc_url' title=''>Welcome Packet from a previous bride<\/a><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Day Passes are $90 USD for guests who aren't staying at the hotel or vendors such as hair and makeup.\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Local outside photographers are NOT allowed, however you can fly in your photographer and have them stay at the resort as a guest.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <strong>Legal Requirements for those not previously married:<\/strong><\/p> <p> Passport, tourist card, blood tests & four witnesses (and their passports & tourist cards)<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Valid passports. In case the bride's name is not the same in her passport than in her birth certificate and she wants to get married with the same name of her birth certificate she should bring her birth certificate (original) apostilled by the government of her country and translated into Spanish by a Mexican official translator (stamped). Driver license will not be accepted by the official.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> If the bride is widowed or divorced is necessary to bring her birth certificate (original) apostilled by the government of her country and translated into Spanish by a Mexican official translator (stamped), according to Mexican Law the bride must be 12 months divorced before remarrying.<span  style=\"font-size: 12px\"> <span  style=\"color: #333333\"><span  style=\"font-family: tahoma\">In case the bride\u00b4s name is the same as her maiden name in the passport \u00e2\u20ac\u201c she can use the passport as official ID and will marry as single ( In Mexico after being divorce the marital status is single) \u00e2\u20ac\u201c no translations of birth certificate are required.<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span  style=\"font-size: 12px\"><span  style=\"color: #333333\"><span  style=\"font-family: tahoma\">If the groom is widowed or divorced, no additional documents are required (as his name did not change)<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Tourist Card. Travelers get this card upon arrival at the airport in Mexico.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Medical Documentation: Blood tests (Sexually Transmitted diseases - VDRL, HIV, Blood Type) and medical certification stating that all results were negative and patient is physically in good health. Blood tests have to be done here in Mexico, we have a clinic at the Resort - (approximate cost: 90.00 USD per person paid IN CASH).<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Four witnesses: two for the bride and two for the groom with valid passport. The witnesses have to be older than 18 years. All witnesses must come in person to the appointment with the wedding coordinator with their valid passport and tourist card at least 4 labor days prior to the wedding date.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/786\/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here\/1940#post_1007105' class='bbc_url' title=''>Post #1945 - It's really THAT easy!<\/a><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <strong>UK Legal Requirements (updated 8\/17\/2012):<\/strong><\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_4_1_1_1345220679318_446\"> Deed Poll (if you have changed your name)<\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_4_1_1_1345220679318_445\"> Adoption Certificate (even if only adopted by step father\/mother)<\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_4_1_1_1345220679318_440\"> Birth Certificates (even from the person who has an adoption certificate).\u00a0In the UK (not sure about other countries) the adoption certificate super seeds the birth certificate... this means that the birth certificate can not be used for any legal \u00a0purpose.. But the Mexican authorities require it... the general registry office in London is very reluctant to produce on of these, but will in the end.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <strong>Ala Carte Information:<\/strong><\/p> <p> If guests stays for 4 or 7 nights how many nights can they eat at the a la cart restaurant?<\/p> <p> 3 or 4 nights 1 dinner<\/p> <p> 5 or 6 nights 2 dinners<\/p> <p> 7 or 9 nights 3 dinners<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> If you take the dinner included in the wedding package, that counts as one of your guests ala carte meals.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <strong>Random Information:<\/strong><\/p> <p> The bars located by the pool and beach area close at 5:00 pm , bars located in the lobby from 10 am till 11:00 pm Music Bar from 6:30 pm till 10:30 pm , Bars located at Hacienda Do\u00b1a Isabel from 7:00 pm till midnight and Disco from midnight till 2:00 am<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Everything is paid for at the end of your stay, and they do accept credit cards. (Except the blood work, that is in cash at the time of your appointment)<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> The internet access is at the Hacienda so you have to pay in cash (it can't be charged to the room - I don't think). I used it once for under 10 minutes and I think it was close to $7-8 (so about $1\/min). I don't remember exactly though. I paid in USD but they take pesos too.\u00a0 Diamond club members get free internet access in the lobby.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Brides and Grooms are given Gold bracelets, my family all were \"Gold class\" but got yellow bracelets. As it was explained to us, actual gold bracelets are VIP. They do not keep track of your a la cartes.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Rehearsals aren\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t done at this resort.\u00a0 But the coordinators will not let you screw up.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Legal ceremonies cannot be altered and must be read in Spanish and translated to English.\u00a0 You can add readings or sand ceremony type items after the legal portion has been completed.\u00a0 This can either be read by the translator or a guest.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/786\/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here\/1360#post_743274' class='bbc_url' title=''>Here is a post where some additional random questions are answered<\/a><\/p> <p> <a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/786\/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here\/1360#post_743274' class='bbc_url' title=''>Here too.<\/a><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Hotel safe = $6 extra a day.\u00a0 Some people have gotten this as a perk, some people haven't.\u00a0 Just be prepared to pay it and be pleasantly surprised if you don't have to.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Mosquitoes in October\/November<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> All three resorts now use key cards instead of traditional keys.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Hurricane Information:<\/p> <p> In 2011 Tropical Storm Rina hit the Gran Bahia.\u00a0 In the days leading up to landfall it was a Hurricane 2 and then a 1.\u00a0 One of our brides was visiting the resort at this time has reported back:<\/p> <p> \"I have never been exposed to really bad weather there and have to say the Bahia kept us well informed about the path of the storm and how that would affect the hotel and guests. They prepared for the worst but it ended up being not too bad. They pulled the hurricane shutters, evacuated Building 66 at Akumal (right on the beach), removed all lounge chairs from the beach and pool areas, removed signage\/garbage cans etc that could be blown around or damaged.<\/p> <p> They removed strips of thatching from the Grand Tortuga roof to allow the wind to blow through...and then repaired it when the storm passed.<\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_4_1_3_1321279261041_21\"> They did the same thing with the Premier Lobby bordering Coba and Akumal. It was good to experience how they handle such weather\/storms...I always felt safe and well informed.\"<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"~Trisha~<br \/>\n<a class='bbc_url' href='http:\/\/www.faberphotography.com'>www.faberphotography.com<\/a><br \/>\n<br \/>\nMy latest destination wedding photos can be found <a class='bbc_url' href='http:\/\/faberphotography.com\/destination-wedding\/'>HERE<\/a>","Email":"tfaber@wbmi.com","IpAddress":"12.24.226.126","GroupId":46,"GroupName":"VIP Member","JoinDate":1171980900,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-207201.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Tlseege","Id":207201,"Name":"Tlseege","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":63282,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"40c5853b8a64373a9975d3460ae8341f","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wedding Packages 2014&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/u&gt;.&amp;nbsp; If you are sent a more up to date version, please PM me.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/786\/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here\/2330#post_1124798\"&gt;Post #2333&lt;\/a&gt; has the Civil Ceremony Order&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=\"display:none\"&gt;iliv Wedding Pkia&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;\/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SUNSHINE - $1,490 (Legal ceremony) $1345 (Symbolic ceremony)&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Civil wedding (judge fees, marriage license and certificate.) **WHEN LEGAL WEDDING**&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Minister\u00b4s Fee ** When Symbolic Wedding ( non legal) \u00e2\u20ac\u201c Renewal of Vows**&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Marriage ceremony with music from CD.(couple may bring their own).&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Romantic Ornamental decoration of the wedding site, location will be assigned after arrival.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Picturesque Wedding location \u00e2\u20ac\u201c may be celebrated on the beach or gazebo (upon confirmation)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Music for the Ceremony with recorded CD ( couple may bring their own)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Bride &amp;amp; Groom\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s bouquet &amp;amp; boutonniere (Tropical Local Flowers) \u00e2\u20ac\u201c just for the couple. &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Domestic sparkling wine celebration toast after the ceremony (1 bottle per 7 adults, maximum total of&amp;nbsp; 4 bottles)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Sit down dinner in one of our restaurants with set menu ( semi private)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Standard Wedding Cake for all wedding guests or dessert choice (Dessert from our specialty restaurant menu rather than the traditional wedding cake) &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Room Upgrade for the couple &amp;amp; parents (subject to availability upon arrival). &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Upgraded in-room Amenities (just for the couple)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Transfer to wedding location for the couple. &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Bottle of wine upon arrival in room (wedding couple)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Luxury Turn down service (wedding couple &amp;amp; parents)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;10 professional full digital colored pictures of the wedding ceremony&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;15% Discount on Spa treatments (except pedicure, manicure, hairdresser &amp;amp; makeup)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Late Check out ( wedding couple &amp;amp; parents, upon request at the check in &amp;amp; subject to availability)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Professional Services of an Onsite Wedding Coordinator.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Witnesses (if required)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;Romantic Decoration in couple room ( welcome surprise)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;VIP treatment for the couple&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p style=\"margin-left:27.0pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:0in\"&gt;\u00b7&lt;span style=\"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;\"&gt;   &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#333333\"&gt;1 Newlywed\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s Romantic breakfast in bed ( just for the couple)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;!--[if gte mso 9]&gt;&lt;xml&gt; &lt;w:WordDocument&gt; &lt;w:View&gt;Normal&lt;\/w:View&gt; &lt;w:Zoom&gt;0&lt;\/w:Zoom&gt; &lt;w:TrackMoves\/&gt; &lt;w:TrackFormatting\/&gt; &lt;w:PunctuationKerning\/&gt; &lt;w:ValidateAgainstSchemas\/&gt; &lt;w:SaveIfXMLInvalid&gt;false&lt;\/w:SaveIfXMLInvalid&gt; &lt;w:IgnoreMixedContent&gt;false&lt;\/w:IgnoreMixedContent&gt; &lt;w:AlwaysShowPlaceholderText&gt;false&lt;\/w:AlwaysShowPlaceholderText&gt; &lt;w:DoNotPromoteQF\/&gt; &lt;w:LidThemeOther&gt;EN-US&lt;\/w:LidThemeOther&gt; &lt;w:LidThemeAsian&gt;X-NONE&lt;\/w:LidThemeAsian&gt; &lt;w:LidThemeComplexScript&gt;X-NONE&lt;\/w:LidThemeComplexScript&gt; &lt;w:Compatibility&gt; &lt;w:BreakWrappedTables\/&gt; &lt;w:SnapToGridInCell\/&gt; &lt;w:WrapTextWithPunct\/&gt; &lt;w:UseAsianBreakRules\/&gt; &lt;w:DontGrowAutofit\/&gt; &lt;w:SplitPgBreakAndParaMark\/&gt; &lt;w:EnableOpenTypeKerning\/&gt; &lt;w:DontFlipMirrorIndents\/&gt; &lt;w:OverrideTableStyleHps\/&gt; &lt;\/w:Compatibility&gt; &lt;w:BrowserLevel&gt;MicrosoftInternetExplorer4&lt;\/w:BrowserLevel&gt; &lt;m:mathPr&gt; &lt;m:mathFont m:val=\"Cambria Math\"\/&gt; &lt;m:brkBin m:val=\"before\"\/&gt; &lt;m:brkBinSub m:val=\"&#45;-\"\/&gt; &lt;m:smallFrac m:val=\"off\"\/&gt; &lt;m:dispDef\/&gt; &lt;m:lMargin m:val=\"0\"\/&gt; &lt;m:rMargin m:val=\"0\"\/&gt; &lt;m:defJc m:val=\"centerGroup\"\/&gt; &lt;m:wrapIndent m:val=\"1440\"\/&gt; &lt;m:intLim m:val=\"subSup\"\/&gt; &lt;m:naryLim m:val=\"undOvr\"\/&gt; &lt;\/m:mathPr&gt;&lt;\/w:WordDocument&gt; &lt;\/xml&gt;&lt;![endif]--&gt;&lt;!--[if gte mso 9]&gt;&lt;xml&gt; &lt;w:LatentStyles DefLockedState=\"false\" DefUnhideWhenUsed=\"true\" DefSemiHidden=\"true\" DefQFormat=\"false\" DefPriority=